---
import StaticPageLayout from "../../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
import { contactEmail, globalPaths, siteUrl } from "../../data/site-shell";

const schema = [
	{
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "PrivacyPolicy",
		name: "Privacy Policy",
		url: `${siteUrl}${globalPaths.privacy}`,
	},
	{
		"@context": "https://schema.org",
		"@type": "BreadcrumbList",
		itemListElement: [
			{
				"@type": "ListItem",
				position: 1,
				name: "Home",
				item: siteUrl,
			},
			{
				"@type": "ListItem",
				position: 2,
				name: "Privacy Policy",
				item: `${siteUrl}${globalPaths.privacy}`,
			},
		],
	},
];
---

<StaticPageLayout
	title="Privacy Policy - Her Trees Puzzle Dream"
	description="Privacy information for the Her Trees Puzzle Dream play hub, including analytics, embeds, and contact requests."
	canonicalPath={globalPaths.privacy}
	pageHeading="Privacy Policy"
	pageIntro="This page explains what information treespuzzle.com may process, how that information is used, and how to contact the site about privacy-related concerns."
	breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
	schema={schema}
>
	<p>
		treespuzzle.com is a content website. It does not require an account to read
		pages, and it does not ask visitors to create a login profile. Even so, the
		website may process limited technical information in the normal course of
		operating pages, measuring site performance, and handling direct contact
		requests. This policy is written to help visitors understand that limited data
		use in plain language.
	</p>
	<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
	<p>
		Like most websites, this site may receive technical information sent by a
		browser or device when a page is loaded. That can include an IP address, device
		or browser type, approximate location derived from the network, referring page,
		language settings, and timestamps. Server or hosting logs may temporarily store
		some of this information for security, debugging, and traffic analysis.
	</p>
	<p>
		The homepage also uses Microsoft Clarity to better understand high-level site
		usage patterns such as page interaction, scrolling, and aggregate engagement.
		Clarity may use cookies or similar technologies to collect usage information
		and session data. That information helps identify broken layouts, weak
		navigation, or sections that are not useful to visitors.
	</p>
	<h3>Embeds and third-party services</h3>
	<p>
		Some pages embed or link to third-party content, including YouTube video
		players, storefront pages, and browser-playable game content. When you use
		those services, the third party may collect information under its own privacy
		policy. treespuzzle.com does not control those third-party practices and cannot
		guarantee how an external platform uses data once you interact with it.
	</p>
	<p>
		External services linked from the site may include Steam, itch.io, YouTube, or
		other platforms used to distribute or discuss the HER TREES games. You should
		review the privacy terms of those services directly if you choose to use them.
	</p>
	<h3>Contact information and requests</h3>
	<p>
		If you email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>, the site
		may keep your message, email address, and any related discussion for the
		purpose of responding, handling corrections, or addressing rights-related
		issues. Contact correspondence may be retained as long as reasonably necessary
		to resolve the issue or maintain an accurate administrative record.
	</p>
	<h3>How information is used</h3>
	<p>
		Information described above may be used to operate the site, understand traffic
		patterns, improve content quality, respond to requests, prevent abuse, and
		maintain basic security. The site does not sell visitor personal information.
		If advertising is added in the future, this policy may be updated to describe
		additional data practices that relate to ad delivery, consent, or measurement.
	</p>
	<h3>Your choices</h3>
	<p>
		You can limit certain forms of browser tracking through browser settings,
		cookie controls, private browsing, or extensions that block analytics and
		third-party scripts. If you have a privacy concern tied specifically to this
		site, email the address above with enough detail to identify the page and the
		nature of the request.
	</p>
</StaticPageLayout>
